The learner submits in two steps: Validate answers parses the current fields and displays the expression form (for example, x+x rather than a simplified 2*x), then Check answer grades that validated response. Editing any field invalidates the preview, so the learner must validate again. This explicit check mirrors the question input verification setting and helps learners catch syntax errors before grading. The polynomial example sets &lt;insertstars&gt;1&lt;/insertstars&gt;, so x**2+8x+15 previews as one sum and receives full credit in its first variant.
