The options are file and question (required), seed (signed integer, default 1), variants (1–20, default 1), review (true or false, default false), and diagnostics (true or false, default false). feedback: true opts a card into the shared AI Feedback extension; cards without it need no AI dependency. Install both extensions in the same project. context: auto (default) uses nearby visible prose; context: none omits it; context: id1,id2 includes tagged blocks such as ::: {#id1 .ai-context} (.ai-feedback-context and .math-exercise-context are shared aliases). feedback-language sets the explanation language (default document lang). feedback-policy selects an existing named policy from ai-feedback.policy-files or page policy files. A stable label targets exercise-specific policy settings; otherwise the card ID is used. The shared mathematics policy (math-exercise) supplies the default hints and is also the YAML integration namespace for STACK cards. A fixed seed reproduces a variant within this implementation. It does not promise the same pseudo-random sequence as Moodle’s Maxima backend.
Feedback uses a learner’s current answer, visible question text and selected context. A preceding matching Check answer can contribute minimal result status, finite score; XML, source panels, teacher answers, qtests, grader configuration, grader feedback messages and answer notes are excluded. It never grades a response or replaces Validate answers and Check answer. The shared settings panel lets a learner choose copy-prompt mode or configure their own compatible provider; no API key is placed in the page. The same nested YAML policy layers are inherited across integrations, using math-exercise for STACK’s mathematics policy namespace.

